Stellis downloads or calls the following third-party components. They are not
part of this repository and keep their own licences.

Speech models, downloaded by scripts/setup_models.sh
- Whisper "small.en" in ggml format, from whisper.cpp (MIT).
  https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp
- Pyannote segmentation 3.0, ONNX export distributed by sherpa-onnx (MIT).
  https://huggingface.co/pyannote/segmentation-3.0
- NVIDIA NeMo TitaNet small speaker model, ONNX export distributed by
  sherpa-onnx. Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
  (CC BY 4.0). https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Native tools, installed separately by the user
- FFmpeg (https://ffmpeg.org). Builds such as Homebrew's are licensed under
  the GNU General Public License version 3. Stellis runs FFmpeg as a separate
  program and does not include or link it.
- whisper.cpp command-line tool (MIT).

Libraries
- sherpa-onnx (Apache License 2.0).
- Python and JavaScript dependencies listed in pyproject.toml, uv.lock,
  package.json, and package-lock.json, under their own licences.
- Inter and Piazzolla fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1), bundled with their
  licence files in src/stellis/static/fonts.

Sample meetings, downloaded by scripts/load_samples.py
- AMI Meeting Corpus, University of Edinburgh. Licensed under Creative Commons
  Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
  https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/corpus/license.shtml
  The samples are not part of this repository.

Test fixture
- tests/fixtures/jfk.wav is the speech sample distributed with whisper.cpp (MIT).
